        "body": "`getType` looks the extension up as-is, so `/photos/IMG_0001.JPG` or `/LOGO.PNG` gets no type from `serveStatic`. on node the response then goes out as `text/plain; charset=UTF-8`, on web with no content-type at all. uppercase extensions are pretty common for camera uploads.\n\nlowercased the extension before the lookup. the custom `getType` option still gets the extension as written.\n\nadded a test that fails on main for both web and node:\n\n```\nAssertionError: expected 'text/plain; charset=UTF-8' to be 'image/jpeg'\n```\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Uppercase and mixed-case file extensions now resolve to the correct MIME type.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
