        "body": "Fixes #1578\n\n`serveStatic` passes the full request path as `id`, so with `app.use(\"/public/**\")` a request to `/public/index.html` reads `public/public/index.html`, and `/` never matches the route at all. the example 404s on every path, while the text says to open http://localhost:3000.\n\nmounted it at `/**` so it serves `public/` at the root like the text says, and added a tip with `withBase` for serving under a prefix.\n\nran the example against main:\n\n```\napp.use(\"/public/**\")   / -> 404 | /index.html -> 404 | /public/index.html -> 404\napp.use(\"/**\")          / -> 200 | /index.html -> 200\nwithBase(\"/public\")     /public/ -> 200 | /public/index.html -> 200 | /public/nope.txt -> 404\n```\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated static asset examples to match all request paths.\n  * Added guidance on using the full request path and removing the `/public` prefix when serving files from that directory.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
